Z||000000||Philphine||06-12-2001||10:50 AM||||<BR>i think i'm getting one off ebay. it may end up on my chopper if i get anywhere with that project. it would give me space in the instrument pod for other guages... and look neat (ok, i admit i'm a style fiend) anyone seen one on a fiero or maybe had a judge or gto (or ford. didn't really know they had them till i read the ebay ad) with one? how'd you like it? i'm wondering with the hood opening from the rear if it would take battering and jolting of the lid being dropped. also line of sight issues, durability from being exposed to the elements and how visible it would be through a tinted windshield. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroHarry||06-12-2001||11:13 AM||||Isnt your tint at the top of the glass? or have you done something very wild?<P>As too the issue of being outside and putting up with the weather, they made-em-to do just that.<P>If you do this and want something wild and unique (if your worried about damaging the unit by closing the hood),<BR>how about mounting down hard and glassing the hood so as it looks kinda similiar to the old TA shaker hoods (not in the middle of course) but it would never get slammed.<P><BR>Food for thought! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||06-12-2001||11:36 AM||||no tint yet, but my '87 has tint at the top and bottom and i like the look. the slant of the windshield will affect that decision. <P>i know they were meant to go outside but i'm just wondering anyway. they quit doing it that way and i'm hoping it was just a style decision and not something they stopped doing because of durability.<P>i don't have it yet to place on the hood and "eyeball" a location for it but i'm pretty sure it will end up over the front trunk area. i don't think i could cut a hole in it and make it seal well enough around the tach to hard mount it without leaks. i'll keep the idea in the back of my head though. thanks.       ||||reg||1
